    "summary": "I built a seed-starting tray with four cells set side by side in a compact cluster. Each cell holds a half-depth drained bin (hex-bin-half-drain), a shallow bin with drainage holes that suits seed starting. I capped the open outer faces with solid end caps and bolted the joints so the cells can't slide apart. To show it in use, I filled each bin with soil and planted a seedling. The check came back clear: no rule errors and no parts clashing. It comes to 27 printed parts (4 bases, 4 bins, 14 caps and 5 joint bolts), about 1,777 g of filament and roughly 43 hours of printing. The configurator only checks fit, so it can't say how the plastic will stand up to wet soil over time; that depends on the material you print in.",
    "outcome": "built"
  },
